cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the associated LROT study and identify this local code snapshot using its supplied file manifests. The existing collective contributor entry is retained."
title: "LROT: ligand-receptor-guided optimal transport for spatial transcriptomics slice alignment"
abstract: "Reference implementation of LROT, which embeds a manually specified gene-pair compatibility prior as a third cost channel in an entropy-regularised fused Gromov-Wasserstein framework for spatial transcriptomics section alignment, together with locked figure assets and selected saved results; the numerical execution wrapper is source-bound and its portable loading has been verified; fixed-case evidence does not establish full-repository end-to-end reproduction."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "LROT authors"
license: MIT
version: "paper-aligned-release-candidate"
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - optimal transport
  - Gromov-Wasserstein
  - ligand-receptor
  - section alignment
  - 3D reconstruction
